      "message": "Hi,\n\nI saw this call show up in a profile. Is there a reason why you don\u0027t just call lrintf()? It\u0027s single-instruction on most relevant platforms, and will give you the right rounding (at least if “right” is the current rounding mode) for negative values and halfway-between as well, instead of always biasing upwards.\n\n(Unfortunately, on glibc it won\u0027t be inlined without -fno-math-errno, but neither will floorf)",
      "revId": "b9019a730de4349d82c49289f35846369dd80bc0",
